Here is the structured goal model based on the mission description:

### Goal Model

#### Goals

| Name       | Text                                                                                     | Runtime  | Goal Type   | Relation | Justification                                                                 |
|------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|------------|----------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| G1         | Fulfill Resource Request                                                               | -        | Perform    | -        | The mission is about executing the collection and delivery of resources.       |
| G2         | Execute Collection Phase                                                               | #        | Perform    | AND      | Both collection and delivery phases must complete for mission success.       |
| G3         | Execute Delivery Phase                                                                 | #        | Perform    | AND      | Both phases are necessary for the mission to be fulfilled.                   |
| G2.1       | Collect Resource from Storage A                                                        | FALLBACK | Perform    | OR       | If one robot fails, another takes over, ensuring resource collection.         |
| G2.2       | Collect Resource from Storage B                                                        | FALLBACK | Perform    | OR       | Multiple robots can collect from different storages in parallel.             |
| G3.1       | Deliver Resource to Destination A                                                      | FALLBACK | Perform    | OR       | If a robot fails, another continues, ensuring delivery completion.            |
| G3.2       | Deliver Resource to Destination B                                                      | FALLBACK | Perform    | OR       | Multiple delivery points can be handled in parallel by different robots.     |

#### Tasks

| Name       | Text                                                                                     | Relation | Location               | Number of Robots | Justification                                                                 |
|------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|------------------------|-----------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| AT2.1.1    | Navigate to Storage A                                                                  | AND      | Storage A              | 1               | Single robot assigned to collect from Storage A.                           |
| AT2.1.2    | Request Resource from Storage A                                                        | AND      | Storage A              | 1               | Robot must specify resources and wait for retrieval.                        |
| AT3.1.1    | Navigate to Destination A                                                              | AND      | Destination A           | 1               | Single robot delivers to Destination A.                                      |
| AT3.1.2    | Deliver Resource to Destination A                                                      | AND      | Destination A           | 1               | Robot completes delivery after receiving confirmation.                      |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**
  - Justification: Both collection and delivery phases are essential for mission success.

- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2 [OR]**
  - Justification: Multiple robots can collect resources from different storages in parallel.

- **G2.1 -> AT2.1.1, AT2.1.2 [AND]**
  - Justification: A single robot must navigate to the storage and request resources sequentially.

- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 [OR]**
  - Justification: Multiple robots can deliver to different destinations in parallel.

This model ensures that the mission is executed efficiently, with fallback mechanisms in place for battery issues, and leverages parallel execution to minimize mission time.
